# Server API Conventions

## REST Design

- Resource-oriented URLs: `/api/specs`, `/api/specs/:id`, `/api/specs/:id/edges`.
- HTTP methods: `GET` (read), `POST` (create), `PUT` (full replace), `PATCH` (partial update), `DELETE` (remove).
- Controllers handle HTTP concerns only — delegate business logic to services.

## DTO Naming

- `Create{Resource}Dto` — request body for creation.
- `Update{Resource}Dto` — request body for updates (all fields optional via `PartialType`).
- `{Resource}ResponseDto` — shaped response sent to clients.

## Validation & Documentation

- All DTOs use `class-validator` decorators (`@IsString`, `@IsOptional`, `@MinLength`, etc.).
- Add Swagger decorators: `@ApiTags`, `@ApiOperation`, `@ApiResponse` on controllers.
- Consistent response envelope: `{ data, meta? }` for collections, plain object for singles.

## Example

```typescript
import { Controller, Post, Body, UseGuards } from '@nestjs/common';
import { ApiTags, ApiOperation } from '@nestjs/swagger';
import { JwtAuthGuard } from '../auth/jwt-auth.guard.js';
import { CreateSpecDto } from './dto/create-spec.dto.js';
import { SpecService } from './spec.service.js';

@ApiTags('specs')
@Controller('api/specs')
export class SpecController {
  constructor(private readonly specService: SpecService) {}

  @Post()
  @UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard)
  @ApiOperation({ summary: 'Create a new spec' })
  async create(@Body() dto: CreateSpecDto) {
    return this.specService.create(dto);
  }
}
```
